---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<Base title="Ice Hockey Shifts: Support" description="Help and support for the Ice Hockey Shifts iPhone app.">
  <section class="top narrow prose">
    <p class="meta kicker">Ice Hockey Shifts</p>
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p>Ice Hockey Shifts shows the games recorded by the Ice Hockey Shifts app for Garmin watches: every
    shift on a timeline, heart-rate zones split between the ice and the bench, and your heart rate through
    the game.</p>

    <h2>Getting a game into the app</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Record a game with Ice Hockey Shifts on your Garmin watch and let it sync to Garmin Connect.</li>
      <li>Export the activity's original file. On the Garmin Connect website, open the activity, then the
      gear menu, then <em>Export Original</em>. This gives a <code>.zip</code>.</li>
      <li>Save it to Files on your iPhone (for example with AirDrop or iCloud Drive), then tap <em>Import</em>
      in Ice Hockey Shifts and pick the <code>.zip</code> or <code>.fit</code>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Activities recorded by other apps open with heart rate only, because only Ice Hockey Shifts marks
    which laps were shifts.</p>

    <h2>Why does it ask how many players were dressed?</h2>
    <p>Your fair share of ice time depends on how many defence (or forwards) dressed that night, and no file
    records it. The answer is saved with the game.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions, bugs or ideas: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    <p><a href="/iceshifts/privacy/">Privacy policy</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
